WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.677
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book one.

2
00:00:04.977 --> 00:00:08.386
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.686 --> 00:00:13.556
Unit one: Daily Routines. In this unit, you will describe your daily routine.

4
00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:15.377
Wake up.

5
00:00:16.077 --> 00:00:18.378
Wake up means to stop sleeping.

6
00:00:18.678 --> 00:00:20.306
I wake up at six o'clock.

7
00:00:21.006 --> 00:00:23.252
Your turn. Say: Wake up.

8
00:00:25.952 --> 00:00:26.861
Wake up.

9
00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:28.816
Get dressed.

10
00:00:29.516 --> 00:00:31.655
Get dressed means to put on your clothes.

11
00:00:31.955 --> 00:00:33.978
I get dressed after my shower.

12
00:00:34.678 --> 00:00:37.725
Your turn. Say: Get dressed.

13
00:00:40.425 --> 00:00:41.542
Get dressed.

14
00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:43.458
Brush teeth.

15
00:00:44.158 --> 00:00:46.878
Brush teeth means to clean your teeth with a toothbrush.

16
00:00:47.178 --> 00:00:49.235
I brush my teeth twice a day.

17
00:00:49.935 --> 00:00:52.738
Your turn. Say: Brush teeth.

18
00:00:55.438 --> 00:00:56.335
Brush teeth.

19
00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:58.142
Homework.

20
00:00:58.842 --> 00:01:01.991
Homework means school work you do at home.

21
00:01:02.291 --> 00:01:04.012
I do my homework after school.

22
00:01:04.712 --> 00:01:07.608
Your turn. Say: Homework.

23
00:01:10.308 --> 00:01:11.170
Homework.

24
00:01:12.183 --> 00:01:13.103
Bedtime.

25
00:01:13.803 --> 00:01:16.209
Bedtime means the time when you go to bed.

26
00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:18.416
My bedtime is nine o'clock.

27
00:01:19.116 --> 00:01:21.722
Your turn. Say: Bedtime.

28
00:01:24.422 --> 00:01:25.260
Bedtime.

29
00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:27.402
Alarm clock.

30
00:01:28.102 --> 00:01:30.937
Alarm clock means a clock that rings to wake you up.

31
00:01:31.237 --> 00:01:33.283
My alarm clock rings at six.

32
00:01:33.983 --> 00:01:37.240
Your turn. Say: Alarm clock.

33
00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:41.115
Alarm clock.

34
00:01:42.117 --> 00:01:42.862
Shower.

35
00:01:43.562 --> 00:01:46.293
Shower means washing your body under running water.

36
00:01:46.593 --> 00:01:48.442
I take a shower every morning.

37
00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:52.270
Your turn. Say: Shower.

38
00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:55.786
Shower.

39
00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:57.726
Uniform.

40
00:01:58.426 --> 00:02:01.703
Uniform means the special clothes students wear at school.

41
00:02:02.003 --> 00:02:04.084
Our uniform is white and blue.

42
00:02:04.784 --> 00:02:07.517
Your turn. Say: Uniform.

43
00:02:10.217 --> 00:02:11.149
Uniform.

44
00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:12.989
Bus stop.

45
00:02:13.689 --> 00:02:16.350
Bus stop means a place where the bus stops for people.

46
00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.162
I wait at the bus stop.

47
00:02:18.862 --> 00:02:21.421
Your turn. Say: Bus stop.

48
00:02:24.121 --> 00:02:25.088
Bus stop.

49
00:02:26.083 --> 00:02:27.073
On foot.

50
00:02:27.773 --> 00:02:29.134
On foot means walking.

51
00:02:29.434 --> 00:02:31.015
I go to school on foot.

52
00:02:31.715 --> 00:02:34.263
Your turn. Say: On foot.

53
00:02:36.963 --> 00:02:38.022
On foot.

54
00:02:39.017 --> 00:02:39.786
Late.

55
00:02:40.486 --> 00:02:42.357
Late means after the right time.

56
00:02:42.657 --> 00:02:44.216
Don't be late for class!

57
00:02:44.916 --> 00:02:47.406
Your turn. Say: Late.

58
00:02:50.106 --> 00:02:50.921
Late.

59
00:02:51.917 --> 00:02:52.860
Punctual.

60
00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:55.443
Punctual means always on time.

61
00:02:55.743 --> 00:02:58.184
Sreypich is always punctual.

62
00:02:58.884 --> 00:03:01.803
Your turn. Say: Punctual.

63
00:03:04.503 --> 00:03:05.377
Punctual.

64
00:03:06.383 --> 00:03:08.476
Now let's listen to a conversation.

65
00:03:08.776 --> 00:03:10.996
Sreypich, what time do you wake up?

66
00:03:12.283 --> 00:03:14.155
I wake up at six o'clock.

67
00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:16.370
What do you do next?

68
00:03:17.683 --> 00:03:20.530
I take a shower, get dressed and brush my teeth.

69
00:03:21.817 --> 00:03:23.166
How do you go to school?

70
00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:26.870
I go on foot. I'm never late!

71
00:03:28.183 --> 00:03:31.564
Grammar focus: Present simple for routines.

72
00:03:31.864 --> 00:03:35.086
I wake up at six. I do my homework after school.

73
00:03:35.386 --> 00:03:40.093
Use the present simple for things you do every day. Add -s with he, she or it.

74
00:03:41.083 --> 00:03:43.829
Now read and listen. A Day in My Life.

75
00:03:44.129 --> 00:03:46.221
My alarm clock rings at six o'clock.

76
00:03:47.517 --> 00:03:50.909
I wake up, take a shower, get dressed and brush my teeth.

77
00:03:52.217 --> 00:03:54.739
I put on my uniform and walk to school on foot.

78
00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:58.595
After school, I do my homework before dinner.

79
00:03:59.883 --> 00:04:03.462
My bedtime is nine o'clock, so I am never late in the morning.

80
00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:07.449
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

81
00:04:07.749 --> 00:04:09.551
She blank up at six every day.

82
00:04:09.851 --> 00:04:13.086
A, wake. B, wakes. C, waking.

83
00:04:17.083 --> 00:04:19.303
The answer is B: wakes.

84
00:04:20.817 --> 00:04:22.538
Always on time means blank.

85
00:04:22.838 --> 00:04:25.945
A, punctual. B, late. C, lazy.

86
00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:32.205
The answer is A: punctual.

87
00:04:33.717 --> 00:04:35.763
I blank my homework after school.

88
00:04:36.063 --> 00:04:39.449
A, do. B, does. C, doing.

89
00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:45.217
The answer is A: do.

90
00:04:46.717 --> 00:04:49.984
Now it's your turn to speak. Describe your typical school day.

91
00:04:55.284 --> 00:05:01.524
I wake up at half past five and take a shower. I go to school by bus, and I do my homework in the evening.

92
00:05:01.824 --> 00:05:03.545
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

93
00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:09.048
Great work today! You learned twelve new words and present simple for routines.

94
00:05:09.348 --> 00:05:14.067
Today's value is discipline. Follow your routine, even when it is hard.

95
00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:16.764
See you in Unit two. Goodbye!

96
00:05:17.064 --> 00:05:19.438
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

